step Engineering recipes at 30
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Handful of Copper Bolts (from 30, 1s 15c). Also learn Reagent Bot (1s): Forever's Engineering camp item, placed at a campsite beside a campfire. It takes a Handful of Copper Bolts and a Copper Tube, which you learn at 30 and 50, so it gives no points. The Camping 101: Engineering quest from your starting area's camping guide (after The Great Outdoors) sends you to an engineering trainer who teaches it free. Train Journeyman Mining on this visit too: it raises Mining's cap to 150, needs Mining 50 and costs 5s (the arrow picks the nearest Mining trainer of your faction).
  learn 3922
  learn 1230656
  train Mining Journeyman

step Handful of Copper Bolts to 59
  tip Handful of Copper Bolts is orange at 30 (yellow 45, green 52, grey 60): about 50 crafts to 59, up to 63 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Copper Bar. One Copper Bar a craft. Keep the bolts: Practice Locks and later gadgets take them. Needs an anvil nearby. Blacksmith Hammer is a tool: keep it in your bags.
  craft 3922 until 59

step Mine Copper Ore, smelt Copper Bar (Mining 50-57)
  tip 38 Copper Bar for Engineering 59-75: 16 Copper Tubes. Mine 38 Copper Ore (Mining 50 to 57), smelt 38 Copper Bar at a forge, then craft 16 Copper Tubes (Engineering 59 to 75). The window lists the Mining areas for your level, best first: the arrow leads to the one you pick and rests there until your bags hold them.
  collect 2840 x101 gather Mining 50
